WEBVTT

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:18.100
I'm finished mepo!

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.200
The other day was terrible.

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:33.750
Honoka's parents had come 
home for the first time

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:36.430
in a year to celebrate Honoka's birthday, but

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:38.750
they were caught in the middle of a robbery.

00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:47.590
And that muscular, menacing 
man came to attack us again.

00:00:47.590 --> 00:00:48.860
It really was the pits.

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:55.770
But in the end, Honoka seemed happy, so

00:00:55.770 --> 00:00:57.420
I guess I'm a little relieved.

00:00:57.860 --> 00:00:58.910
Sis!

00:01:01.630 --> 00:01:03.060
What do you want, Ryota?

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:06.000
You can have my share of 
strawberries for dessert.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.780
What brought this on?

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:09.720
I don't have any money 
if that's what you want.

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:11.580
I've already gotten an 
advance on my allowance.

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:13.250
It's nothing like that.

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:16.420
Actually, I wanted you to 
take me to the aquarium.

00:01:17.030 --> 00:01:18.320
The aquarium?

00:01:19.490 --> 00:01:21.960
<i>Pretty Cure! Pretty Cure!</i>

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:24.630
<i>Pretty Cure Pretty Cure</i>

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:27.400
<i>Pretty Cure Pretty Cure</i>

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:31.870
<i>We're pretty and cure cure Together we are...</i>

00:01:31.870 --> 00:01:34.570
<i>PRETTY CURE...!</i>

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:37.710
<i>Out of the frying pan, into the fire</i>

00:01:37.810 --> 00:01:39.310
<i>Frankly, it's totally unbelievable</i>

00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:43.310
<i>Even in our school in our 
school uniforms, we're both</i>

00:01:43.510 --> 00:01:45.120
<i>amazingly tough</i>

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:50.920
<i>Each time we get out of a tight spot,</i>

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:52.890
<i>we both</i>

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:54.230
<i>become stronger</i>

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:56.790
<i>and closer</i>

00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:00.800
<i>Yeah! Your best! My best! Because we're alive</i>

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:03.370
<i>we never fail!</i>

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:06.540
<i>Don't you know that good fortune</i>

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:09.110
<i>comes to the gates of laughter?
Out with the negative!</i>

00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:15.280
<i>Brighten up your life!
Try with all your might...</i>

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:16.580
<i>Work like the devil!</i>

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:19.050
<i>Pretty Cure! Pretty Cure!</i>

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:22.090
<i>Pretty Cure! Pretty Cure!</i>

00:02:22.090 --> 00:02:26.360
<i>We're pretty and cure cure Together we are</i>

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:29.430
<i>Pretty Cure!</i>

00:02:29.630 --> 00:02:33.160
<i>Pretty Cure! Pretty Cure!</i>

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:38.280
I have to write about fish 
for my science homework.

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:40.640
So take me to the aquarium 
this coming Sunday.

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:41.840
Too bad.

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:46.240
I promised Shiho and the others that 
I'd go out with them on Sunday.

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:49.830
Mom told me to get you to take me.

00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:51.310
No... No... No...!

00:02:52.170 --> 00:02:55.450
Mom! Nagisa said she won't take me.

00:02:55.450 --> 00:02:58.920
Nagisa! Why don't you act like 
a big sister once in a while?

00:02:58.920 --> 00:02:59.890
But...

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:03.680
On Sunday, your dad is working, 
and I have something that

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:06.500
I can't get out of, too.

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:09.800
But I have things to do, too.

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:11.300
You're just going to play, aren't you?

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:14.220
So, please! Take him.

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:16.770
Stop complaining.

00:03:17.270 --> 00:03:18.410
All right.

00:03:18.410 --> 00:03:19.740
Yes!

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:22.110
Those are my strawberries!

00:03:22.110 --> 00:03:24.180
Aw, don't be like that.

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:25.350
Why, you little...!

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:28.290
Cobra twist!

00:03:30.820 --> 00:03:32.290
That was a great bath.

00:03:32.590 --> 00:03:34.350
Help me, Dad!

00:03:34.350 --> 00:03:37.800
Nagisa... For the cobra twist, 
you use your left arm to

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:41.510
hold Ryota's right arm 
down, and stretch his body.

00:03:41.510 --> 00:03:42.590
That's it.

00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:44.100
Get me some milk.

00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:51.680
I give... give up!

00:03:55.130 --> 00:03:59.680
"SAVE RYOTA! GEKIDRAGO PANIC"

00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:58.510
"SAVE RYOTA! GEKIDRAGO PANIC"

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:05.560
This is exciting.

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:08.040
I had no idea you loved aquariums, Honoka.

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:09.870
I knew I could count on you.

00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:11.460
I'm glad you came along.

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:12.860
Let's go, Honoka-san.

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:18.540
Honoka-san? He's getting carried away.

00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:24.240
You seem depressed, Gekidrago.

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:26.160
What did you expect?

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:30.060
After failing so many times, 
anyone would be depressed.

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:33.870
Then your only choice is to 
return to the darkness now.

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:35.880
Before they do you in.

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:36.800
Stop it.

00:04:37.700 --> 00:04:39.590
What good is it to fight among yourselves?

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:46.030
Use that anger and frustration against them.

00:04:57.460 --> 00:04:59.980
Don't you have the Prism Stones yet?

00:05:01.460 --> 00:05:01.980
Uga.

00:05:02.580 --> 00:05:06.650
Dotsuku Zone needs all seven 
Prism Stones in order to

00:05:06.650 --> 00:05:09.420
take over all of the worlds.

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:13.260
You have no more chances, Gekidrago.

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:17.060
Use up all the power that you have.

00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:27.680
They have almost all things 
that live in the ocean here.

00:05:28.410 --> 00:05:32.680
The quality and temperature of the 
water are all controlled by computer.

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:36.530
They've recreated the 
environment so it's the same

00:05:36.530 --> 00:05:39.180
as the fish's natural environment.

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:44.520
This is a purple tube-dwelling anemone...

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:46.420
Those are upside-down catfish.

00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:47.550
They're strange.

00:05:47.550 --> 00:05:49.250
They're swimming upside-down.

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:52.230
Those are moon jellyfish 
and a spotted jellyfish.

00:05:52.230 --> 00:05:54.200
It hurts if you get stung by them.

00:05:54.710 --> 00:05:56.590
That's a green sea turtle...

00:05:57.430 --> 00:05:59.640
And those are sucker fish whose 
specialty is hitchhiking.

00:06:00.620 --> 00:06:01.910
Kissing gourami...

00:06:01.910 --> 00:06:03.160
They're cute!

00:06:03.160 --> 00:06:05.880
Just what you'd expect from 
a much-talked about aquarium.

00:06:06.150 --> 00:06:09.850
I'm going to study so I'm 
as good as you, Honoka-san.

00:06:10.210 --> 00:06:10.960
Nagisa!

00:06:10.960 --> 00:06:12.120
Honoka!

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:12.870
Mipple!

00:06:12.870 --> 00:06:13.790
Mepple!

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:15.850
I missed you mepo.

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:16.950
I missed you, too mipo.

00:06:18.890 --> 00:06:21.730
Good grief! Will you be quiet!

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:23.190
Where are we mepo?

00:06:28.150 --> 00:06:30.340
That fish looks like a bunch of leaves mepo.

00:06:30.770 --> 00:06:33.570
There are a lot of unusual fish here mipo.

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:40.130
Come here a minute!

00:06:40.130 --> 00:06:41.820
What is this fish called?

00:06:42.100 --> 00:06:43.610
It's a turbot.

00:06:43.610 --> 00:06:46.080
It's really delicious if you deep-fry it.

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:48.050
It tastes good grilled, too.

00:06:48.370 --> 00:06:51.020
It's not a turbot, it's a halibut.

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:53.990
They say, "Left halibut, right turbot."

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:57.960
If the eyes are on the left 
side, it's a halibut...

00:06:58.280 --> 00:07:00.500
If that's a halibut, then 
it would be best as sashimi.

00:07:01.540 --> 00:07:06.330
If Honoka-san was my sister, 
I'd probably be smarter.

00:07:06.330 --> 00:07:10.680
Who do you think made it possible for 
you to come to the aquarium anyway?

00:07:11.790 --> 00:07:13.210
I'm against violence!

00:07:14.270 --> 00:07:15.980
Ouch! Let me go!

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:23.760
Swimming at high speed supplies the tuna with

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:27.230
lots of oxygen from the ocean water,

00:07:27.230 --> 00:07:31.740
so if they don't swim 
continuously, they'll die.

00:07:32.590 --> 00:07:33.930
I'm surprised they don't get tired.

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:38.210
I wonder if that's another species 
that has to swim continuously, too.

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:49.920
Sis! Don't walk ahead all by yourself!

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:51.020
Be quiet!

00:07:51.350 --> 00:07:52.860
Uga!

00:07:54.100 --> 00:07:56.410
Today is the end for you two!

00:07:59.640 --> 00:08:02.330
That's a sea pig playing 
with the keeper, isn't it?

00:08:02.690 --> 00:08:04.300
Its eyes are so cute.

00:08:04.640 --> 00:08:08.570
It eats 55 pounds of food everyday.

00:08:09.620 --> 00:08:11.640
It has an even bigger appetite than you, Sis.

00:08:11.640 --> 00:08:12.330
What?

00:08:22.120 --> 00:08:23.600
That's so cool!

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:24.540
That's a manta ray.

00:08:24.540 --> 00:08:27.290
It's called "oniitomakiei" in Japanese.

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:34.570
What's that?

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:36.570
Don't run!

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:53.630
Wow! Look at that!

00:08:53.630 --> 00:08:54.950
They can do all kinds of things.

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:16.030
Look at all the sharks!

00:09:16.210 --> 00:09:17.840
They're really powerful, aren't they?

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:26.080
It's so huge!

00:09:32.020 --> 00:09:36.520
Don't worry! The glass won't break.

00:10:19.600 --> 00:10:21.490
Attention, everyone!

00:10:21.490 --> 00:10:23.640
A tank in the aquarium has broken...

00:10:23.640 --> 00:10:26.330
It's extremely dangerous, so please 
follow the instructions of the

00:10:26.330 --> 00:10:28.200
people in charge, and 
quickly leave the building.

00:10:36.250 --> 00:10:37.270
What is this?

00:10:37.840 --> 00:10:38.590
Get out of our way!

00:10:38.590 --> 00:10:41.430
Don't! Moray eels are poisonous.

00:10:41.430 --> 00:10:42.810
That can't be!

00:10:44.440 --> 00:10:45.920
Even the snapping turtle...

00:10:45.920 --> 00:10:47.060
Don't tell me, it's...

00:10:47.060 --> 00:10:48.100
Probably.

00:10:48.100 --> 00:10:49.620
What are you talking about?

00:10:52.280 --> 00:10:54.340
It doesn't look like we 
can get out from here.

00:10:54.700 --> 00:10:56.120
Let's look for an emergency exit.

00:10:56.510 --> 00:10:57.440
Let's hurry!

00:11:04.390 --> 00:11:06.940
It's a little sucker fish.

00:11:28.560 --> 00:11:29.590
Stop, Ryota!

00:11:30.450 --> 00:11:32.850
We'll look for an emergency exit, so

00:11:32.850 --> 00:11:34.540
hide over here until we find one.

00:11:35.980 --> 00:11:38.010
But I'll be all alone.

00:11:38.410 --> 00:11:41.360
Don't worry... We'll come right back.

00:11:42.020 --> 00:11:43.510
You'll really come back right away?

00:11:44.560 --> 00:11:45.980
Come on... Hide over here.

00:11:46.300 --> 00:11:48.450
Be sure you don't come out.

00:11:50.910 --> 00:11:51.660
Sis...

00:12:22.480 --> 00:12:24.350
You! All of this...

00:12:24.350 --> 00:12:26.560
...was your doing, wasn't it?

00:12:26.560 --> 00:12:29.860
That's right! Just hand 
over the Prism Stones!

00:12:30.170 --> 00:12:31.330
What if we said "no"?

00:12:31.330 --> 00:12:33.480
Excellent! Great!

00:12:51.940 --> 00:12:53.120
What's going to happen?

00:13:02.570 --> 00:13:03.230
Nagisa!

00:13:03.230 --> 00:13:03.970
Honoka!

00:13:03.970 --> 00:13:05.030
This is terrible mepo!

00:13:05.620 --> 00:13:08.320
All the sinister powers are 
gathering together mepo.

00:13:08.520 --> 00:13:10.760
What do you mean by "sinister powers"?

00:13:11.210 --> 00:13:12.870
It's awesome power mipo!

00:13:20.070 --> 00:13:21.250
What is that?

00:13:21.570 --> 00:13:23.620
A manta ray, shark, and moray eels?

00:13:27.440 --> 00:13:28.590
That's creepy.

00:13:28.880 --> 00:13:31.620
This is my final form!

00:13:31.620 --> 00:13:34.560
Don't take me lightly!

00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:55.410
It's too scary mipo!

00:13:55.650 --> 00:13:57.180
Hurry, and transform mepo!

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:14.330
Dual Aurora Wave!

00:15:10.210 --> 00:15:12.490
Protector of the Light, Cure Black!

00:15:12.990 --> 00:15:15.360
Protector of the Light, Cure White!

00:15:17.640 --> 00:15:19.230
Together, we're Pretty Cure!

00:15:20.650 --> 00:15:22.630
Servants of the power of darkness...

00:15:23.670 --> 00:15:26.070
Go back to where you came from!

00:15:26.940 --> 00:15:30.310
Do you think you can fight against my power?

00:15:30.310 --> 00:15:33.040
Hand over the Prism Stones!

00:15:55.850 --> 00:15:58.100
Sis? Sis!

00:15:58.100 --> 00:15:58.770
Honoka-san?

00:16:23.090 --> 00:16:24.500
What is that?

00:16:26.980 --> 00:16:28.030
Ryota!

00:16:28.030 --> 00:16:29.060
Ryota-kun...

00:16:29.060 --> 00:16:29.890
Ryota...

00:16:38.500 --> 00:16:39.710
Ryota!

00:16:40.710 --> 00:16:41.780
Ryota...

00:16:59.210 --> 00:17:01.590
I'm sorry I dragged you into this...

00:17:02.760 --> 00:17:06.400
How could you involve a little boy like this?

00:17:06.400 --> 00:17:07.560
I won't forgive you.

00:17:09.950 --> 00:17:12.240
Ryota has nothing to do with this.

00:17:12.240 --> 00:17:15.150
If anything happens to Ryota, 
you'll live to regret it!

00:17:15.150 --> 00:17:16.250
Black.

00:17:17.330 --> 00:17:19.620
I won't forgive you!

00:17:23.910 --> 00:17:26.560
Hand over the Prism Stones!

00:17:26.850 --> 00:17:29.920
If you want it that badly, then just take it!

00:17:31.620 --> 00:17:32.730
You're kidding mepo!

00:17:56.640 --> 00:17:58.620
I'm going to blast you out of here!

00:18:09.590 --> 00:18:10.550
How could you...

00:18:10.550 --> 00:18:11.910
How could you do that to my Ryota?

00:18:11.910 --> 00:18:12.370
Now!

00:18:14.320 --> 00:18:15.810
Black Thunder!

00:18:16.340 --> 00:18:18.280
White Thunder!

00:18:26.730 --> 00:18:29.520
The beautiful souls of Pretty Cure...!

00:18:29.950 --> 00:18:32.360
...will crush the sinister hearts!

00:18:38.300 --> 00:18:41.530
Pretty Cure Marble Screw!

00:18:57.450 --> 00:18:59.240
The Prism Stones...

00:18:59.240 --> 00:19:02.420
I'm going to get the Prism Stones!

00:19:04.060 --> 00:19:06.480
I've had enough of this!

00:19:11.930 --> 00:19:15.620
Jyaku-King, sir!

00:19:27.070 --> 00:19:29.680
Zakenna!

00:19:30.130 --> 00:19:33.670
Gomenna! Gomenna! Gomenna!

00:19:36.060 --> 00:19:37.220
Is it over?

00:20:01.910 --> 00:20:03.570
A Prism Stone...?

00:20:08.590 --> 00:20:09.380
Ryota!

00:20:11.930 --> 00:20:12.680
Ryota?

00:20:15.030 --> 00:20:16.700
Sis? What happened?

00:20:18.450 --> 00:20:21.600
I seem to remember something 
awesome going on here...

00:20:22.120 --> 00:20:24.440
Why did you come out?

00:20:24.440 --> 00:20:26.700
I told you to stay hidden, didn't I?

00:20:27.290 --> 00:20:31.170
But I was worried about you...

00:20:33.030 --> 00:20:34.340
I'm sorry.

00:20:40.370 --> 00:20:42.210
I'm so sorry.

00:20:49.780 --> 00:20:53.120
We're supposed to swipe the Guardian 
of Prism Stones card, right?

00:21:03.610 --> 00:21:06.020
Did you want something, girls?

00:21:06.540 --> 00:21:08.700
He's as manly as ever.

00:21:08.700 --> 00:21:10.380
That's what's so strange.

00:21:10.800 --> 00:21:12.350
Hurry, and tell me what you want.

00:21:12.620 --> 00:21:14.650
I'll give you the Prism Stone.

00:21:15.060 --> 00:21:18.290
You got another one back?

00:21:18.630 --> 00:21:20.260
Well done! I'm grateful.

00:21:20.640 --> 00:21:24.040
I never expected two of the Prism Stones 
that were taken to come back to us.

00:21:24.040 --> 00:21:25.960
This is truly a miracle.

00:21:25.960 --> 00:21:29.700
Honoka... Nagisa... Thank you so much mipo!

00:21:30.080 --> 00:21:33.270
You don't have to thank us, do they, Honoka?

00:21:34.290 --> 00:21:36.380
Do you best from now on!

00:21:36.380 --> 00:21:37.930
I bid you goodbye.

00:21:39.060 --> 00:21:40.550
Don't you have a gift for us this time?

00:21:42.120 --> 00:21:43.010
See you again.

00:21:44.310 --> 00:21:45.720
Hello...

00:21:47.060 --> 00:21:48.520
You're here, too, Sis?

00:21:48.520 --> 00:21:51.940
What are you doing here anyway?

00:21:51.940 --> 00:21:56.460
I finished my homework, so I wanted 
Honoka-san to look it over for me.

00:21:56.660 --> 00:21:58.760
When I haven't even seen it yet?

00:21:59.320 --> 00:22:04.380
Even if I showed it to you, all you'll 
say is that it tastes good deep fried.

00:22:04.380 --> 00:22:05.330
What's that?

00:22:05.330 --> 00:22:06.770
Stop that! Not here!

00:22:09.210 --> 00:22:10.010
Give... I give up!

00:22:15.870 --> 00:22:17.550
Ryota!

00:22:24.890 --> 00:22:25.460
<i>Let's go!</i>

00:22:26.290 --> 00:22:26.990
<i>Get you!</i>

00:22:26.990 --> 00:22:29.690
<i>L-O-V-E Love Love, get you!</i>

00:22:29.790 --> 00:22:32.430
<i>I can't do this!</i>

00:22:32.660 --> 00:22:35.700
<i>I'd rather be a young lady than a fighter and</i>

00:22:35.700 --> 00:22:38.140
<i>Get you! Into a love love mode</i>

00:22:38.240 --> 00:22:42.270
<i>And melt your body and soul into sweets</i>

00:22:44.810 --> 00:22:47.980
<i>like chocolate parfait or handsome men</i>

00:22:48.050 --> 00:22:51.720
<i>I'm at the age to seriously 
fall head over heels in love</i>

00:22:52.380 --> 00:22:55.450
<i>I wanted to confess my love again today</i>

00:22:56.590 --> 00:22:59.820
<i>For the sake of the earth 
For the sake of everyone</i>

00:22:59.960 --> 00:23:06.460
<i>That's good, too, but haven't 
you forgotten something?</i>

00:23:07.570 --> 00:23:10.840
